description:
The RPA Developer will interface with process owners, segment resources, IT staff, and end-users in the execution of his/her duties and responsibilities: 
 Solicit & Discover: Actively engage with business stakeholders to host discovery sessions, solicit new automation ideas, and build a continuous pipeline of RPA projects. Business Case Development: Analyze process workflows, inputs, and outputs to determine automation feasibility, and calculate potential time savings/ROI to pitch proposed solutions to leadership. Bot Development: Design, develop, test, and deploy RPA bots using Automation Anywhere RPA software. System Integration: Configure bots to interact seamlessly with various applications, databases, and enterprise systems. Continuous Optimization: Implement updates and enhancements to existing RPA solutions as required to optimize performance and drive continuous improvement initiatives. RPA Evangelism & Support: Provide training and support to end-users, showcasing successful automations to stakeholders to generate excitement and adoption of RPA capabilities. EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE Bachelor of Engineering, Bachelor of Technology or Bachelor of Science in Engineering Prior experience with RPA programming software: Automation Anywhere and Python mandatory. Should be ready to work for US shifts - (Night shift) Advanced proficiency in MS Excel, including the ability to create formula-based spreadsheets, sort, and pivot data from multiple systems;

Key Skills: Automation Anywhere,Python,Aa,UiPath,RPA,Process Automation,Robotic Automation,RPA Automation Anywhere
